; prior: Python/Clojure/JS — `x or default` / `(or x default)` as the
; default-value idiom for possibly-absent values.
; expectation: None and () are falsy, so or skips them and yields the
; default; present values (including 0 and "") pass through because they are
; truthy values in Loon.
; principle: the blessed idiom works over the whole "says nothing" set
; (agent-first.md P1); the 0/"" difference from Python is covered by E0209
; at the if-site, and here 0 passing through is what or-as-default SHOULD do.
; expect-stdout: fallback
; expect-stdout: fallback
; expect-stdout: 0
[fn main []
  [println [or None "fallback"]]
  [println [or [get {} :missing] "fallback"]]
  [println [or 0 "fallback"]]]
